From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:45:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dp: keep the CEC logical addresses when the same
 display is detected again

intel_dp_set_edid() starts with intel_dp_unset_edid(), which calls
drm_dp_cec_unset_edid(): the physical address of the CEC adapter of the
port is invalidated, and the CEC core takes its logical addresses away
(cec_adap_unconfigure(); the adapter needs the HPD, CEC_CAP_NEEDS_HPD,
so it is also disabled). drm_dp_cec_attach() at the end of
intel_dp_set_edid() sets the physical address again, and the core
claims the logical addresses again with polls on the line.

So every detection of a connected display drops the adapter from the
CEC bus for the time of a claim: a probe of the connectors by userspace
(Kodi reads them at its start and after every hot-plug of any display),
a hot-plug of the display, and the polling of the port after an HPD
storm. Meanwhile the adapter acknowledges nothing (the keys of a TV's
remote are lost), drops what it receives, and refuses what userspace
sends (-ENONET). A claim that gets no answer on the line (the port's
IRQ_HPD masked after a storm, a busy line) fails, and the adapter stays
without a logical address until its physical address changes again;
userspace (libCEC) does not ask again.

Seen in issue #24 of LibreELEC Hades: an Intel board whose DisplayPort
output carries CEC through a DisplayPort to HDMI converter; the TV's
remote worked only after a video started, and stopped after another one
that changed the display mode (HLG, HDR), with "HPD interrupt storm
detected on connector DP-1" in the kernel log of that PC.

drm_dp_cec_attach() is made for this (its comment: "If there was a CEC
adapter, then check if the CEC adapter properties were unchanged and
just update the CEC physical address"), and cec_s_phys_addr() does
nothing for the address the adapter has. So intel_dp_set_edid() keeps
the adapter, and only drm_dp_cec_attach() changes its address: the same
one leaves the logical addresses as they are, another one has them
claimed again as before. A display that goes away still invalidates the
address (intel_dp_detect() calls intel_dp_unset_edid() for a port that
is not connected), and the adapter is still unregistered after
drm_dp_cec_unregister_delay where its converter no longer says it can
tunnel CEC.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
index 663af9c..f4e1fe1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
@@ -131,6 +131,7 @@ bool intel_dp_is_edp(struct intel_dp *intel_dp)
 }
 
 static void intel_dp_unset_edid(struct intel_dp *intel_dp);
+static void intel_dp_unset_edid_keep_cec(struct intel_dp *intel_dp);
 
 /* Is link rate UHBR and thus 128b/132b? */
 bool intel_dp_is_uhbr(const struct intel_crtc_state *crtc_state)
@@ -6711,7 +6712,19 @@ intel_dp_set_edid(struct intel_dp *intel_dp)
 	const struct drm_edid *drm_edid;
 	bool vrr_capable;
 
-	intel_dp_unset_edid(intel_dp);
+	/*
+	 * Hades: the CEC adapter of the port is not told that the EDID went away on the way: its
+	 * physical address is set to the one of the new EDID by drm_dp_cec_attach() below, which
+	 * keeps the logical addresses where it is the same. Before, every detection of a
+	 * connected display (a probe of userspace, a hot-plug of the display, the polling of the
+	 * port after an HPD storm) took the logical addresses of the adapter away and had the CEC
+	 * core claim them again on the line; the keys of the TV's remote that came meanwhile were
+	 * not acknowledged, what userspace sent was refused, and a claim that got no answer (an
+	 * HPD storm, a busy line) left the adapter without a logical address until the next
+	 * change of the physical address (issue #24 of LibreELEC Hades: the TV's remote stopped
+	 * after a video that changed the display mode).
+	 */
+	intel_dp_unset_edid_keep_cec(intel_dp);
 	drm_edid = intel_dp_get_edid(intel_dp);
 	connector->detect_edid = drm_edid;
 
@@ -6747,10 +6760,17 @@ intel_dp_set_edid(struct intel_dp *intel_dp)
 
 static void
 intel_dp_unset_edid(struct intel_dp *intel_dp)
+{
+	drm_dp_cec_unset_edid(&intel_dp->aux);
+	intel_dp_unset_edid_keep_cec(intel_dp);
+}
+
+/* Hades: all of intel_dp_unset_edid() but the CEC adapter, for intel_dp_set_edid() */
+static void
+intel_dp_unset_edid_keep_cec(struct intel_dp *intel_dp)
 {
 	struct intel_connector *connector = intel_dp->attached_connector;
 
-	drm_dp_cec_unset_edid(&intel_dp->aux);
 	drm_edid_free(connector->detect_edid);
 	connector->detect_edid = NULL;
 
-- 
2.53.0

